{"latest_judgment":{"docno":"msmarco_v2.1_doc_04_1255404766#1_2577492040","relevance":1,"reason":"This CBS News result is about a type 2 diabetes epidemic among U.S. children, identifying obesity and aggressive disease in young people. It is related background but not Britain/UK-specific and does not address why Britain is becoming an under-40s diabetes capital.","learned":"U.S. youth type 2 diabetes evidence again points to obesity and aggressive disease in young people, but the current crisis/timebomb query is not producing UK-specific direct evidence."},"action":{"op":"query","query":"(^ \"type 2 diabetes\" (+ children \"young people\" adolescents) (+ england uk britain) (+ obesity rise rising diagnosed))","reason":"Search for UK/England evidence on rising type 2 diabetes diagnoses in children and young people with obesity as a driver, likely to produce more direct grade-3 support than the current crisis-framed query."}}
{"request":{"op":"query","query":"(^ \"type 2 diabetes\" (+ children \"young people\" adolescents) (+ england uk britain) (+ obesity rise rising diagnosed))"},"response":{"docno":"msmarco_v2.1_doc_21_502028431#4_1045193672","ok":true,"op":"next","qid":"q530","rank":4,"snippet":"accumulating outside of your cells.” When this happens, “it starts kind of burning, so to say, the entire body,” Shapiro says. “ That’s why you start having issues with your eyes and kidneys and other parts of the body. And even though they have a lot of sugar, your body feels like you’re starving because it’s not going into the cells anywhere,” where it can be used. This creates symptoms of increased hunger and thirst and weight gain that are often associated with Type 2 diabetes. Although Type 2 diabetes has traditionally been rare in children, over the past 30 years or so, rates of this chronic disease have risen significantly among people under 19 years of age. A 2017 study in the New <cover>England Journal of Medicine found that between 2002 and 2012, rates of newly diagnosed cases of Type 2 diabetes in children </cover>aged 10 to 19 increased 4.8 percent each year.\" , \"start_char\": 2220.000000 , \"title\": \"Type 2 Diabetes in Children: Symptoms and Treatments\" , \"url\": \"https://health.usnews.com/conditions/diabetes/diabetes-in-children\" }","skipped":[{"docno":"msmarco_v2.1_doc_46_989687904#0_2148163524","rank":1,"relevance":3},{"docno":"msmarco_v2.1_doc_39_638318757#0_1251334634","rank":2,"relevance":3},{"docno":"msmarco_v2.1_doc_21_502028431#5_1045195931","rank":3,"relevance":1}]}}
