{"latest_judgment":{"docno":"msmarco_v2.1_doc_02_564692629#4_985850250","relevance":3,"reason":"This UK-focused diabetes article directly supports the information need: it says type 2 diabetes usually appears over age 40 but more children, some as young as seven, are now being diagnosed; it also identifies rising obesity, improved diagnosis, and an ageing population as reasons for rising recorded diabetes cases, with Diabetes UK data showing over 80% of type 2 patients are overweight.","learned":"In the UK, type 2 diabetes is increasingly being diagnosed in children despite traditionally appearing after 40; rising obesity and improved diagnosis are cited as key contributors."},"action":{"op":"next","qid":"q531","reason":"The current query is producing UK-focused documents that directly connect obesity, type 2 diabetes, and younger diagnoses, so continuing is likely to yield more grade-3 evidence."}}
{"request":{"op":"next","qid":"q531"},"response":{"docno":"msmarco_v2.1_doc_48_1181377692#1_2146131142","ok":true,"op":"next","qid":"q531","rank":7,"snippet":"2058.000000 , \"headings\": \"Healthy weight loss Healthy weight loss Top tips for healthy weight loss: The problem - overweight and obesity Health benefits of losing weight Weight loss can reduce your risk of: heart disease, stroke, type 2 diabetes and some cancers. BMI and waist circumference Your weight in kilograms (kg) divided by your height in metres (m) squared \" , \"segment\": \"Credit: World Obesity Federation The problem - overweight and <cover>obesity In England, almost 7 out of 10 men and 6 out of 10 women are overweight or obese, and a quarter of adults are obese. Being overweight or obese increases your risk of developing serious diseases such as type 2 diabetes, </cover>coronary heart disease and some cancers. The risks of developing these diseases increases the more overweight you are. Obesity can also affect your quality of life and lead to psychological problems, such as depression and low self-esteem. Ideally it is better to avoid becoming overweight by eating healthily and exercising regularly and maintaining this throughout life. But problems with weight gain are common so here is some information to help you lose weight sensibly and healthily. Your body "}}
