{"latest_judgment":{"docno":"msmarco_v2.1_doc_05_1034556841#1_1877865023","relevance":3,"reason":"This is another passage from a document dedicated to obesity and type 2 diabetes, giving UK-specific evidence that nearly a third of children aged 2–15 in England are obese and that obesity accounts for a very large share of type 2 diabetes risk. It directly supports the main explanation for rising diabetes among younger Britons.","learned":"Public Health England data show high childhood obesity, and obesity is described as accounting for 80–85% of type 2 diabetes risk, supporting obesity as a central driver of young-onset diabetes in Britain."},"action":{"op":"query","query":"(^ \"type 2 diabetes\" \"children\" (+ \"as young as seven\" \"young as seven\" \"age of seven\") (+ uk britain england))","reason":"Search for the UK article/report that says children as young as seven are being diagnosed with type 2 diabetes, which is highly direct evidence for diabetes increasingly affecting the under-40s in Britain."}}
{"request":{"op":"query","query":"(^ \"type 2 diabetes\" \"children\" (+ \"as young as seven\" \"young as seven\" \"age of seven\") (+ uk britain england))"},"response":{"docno":"msmarco_v2.1_doc_02_564692629#3_985848648","ok":true,"op":"next","qid":"q533","rank":2,"snippet":"awareness of the importance of eating a healthy, balanced diet and doing at least 30 minutes of physical activity a day if we want to make any headway in defusing the diabetes time bomb.\" Professor Alan Maryon-Davis, president of the UK Faculty of Public Health, said: \" Early detection and treatment are crucial. We must do whatever we can to find the half-million people who don't know they've got it.\" Rates of obesity and diabetes will continue to rise unless we do something urgently Tam Fry of the National Obesity Forum There are currently over 2.5 million people with diabetes in the <cover>UK and there are more than half a million people with diabetes who have the condition and don't know it. Type 2 diabetes usually appears in people over the age of 40, however, recently, more children are being diagnosed with the condition, some as young as seven.</cover>\" , \"start_char\": 2138.000000 , \"title\": \"BBC NEWS | Health | Rates of diabetes soar in the UK\" , \"url\": \"http://news.bbc.co.uk/2/hi/health/7905734.stm\" }","skipped":[{"docno":"msmarco_v2.1_doc_02_564692629#4_985850250","rank":1,"relevance":3}]}}
