{"request":{"op":"query","query":"(^ \"type 2 diabetes\" \"becoming more common\" \"young people\" (+ lifestyle obesity uk britain england))"},"response":{"docno":"msmarco_v2.1_doc_14_1238729061#4_2534962342","ok":true,"op":"next","qid":"q541","rank":3,"snippet":"1 and Type 2 Self-Check Questions Test Yourself \" , \"segment\": \"Once the pancreas has been removed (because of cancer, for example), diabetes type 1 is always present. Type 2 Diabetes is far more common than type 1. It makes up most of diabetes cases. It usually occurs in adulthood, but <cover>young people are increasingly being diagnosed with this disease. In type 2 diabetes, the pancreas still makes insulin, but the tissues do not respond effectively to normal levels of insulin, a condition termed insulin resistance. Over many years the pancreas will decrease the levels of insulin it secretes, but that is not the main problem when the disease initiates. Many people with type 2 diabetes do not know they have it, although it is a serious condition. Type 2 diabetes is becoming more common due to increasing obesity </cover>and failure to exercise, both of which contribute to insulin resistance. Self-Check Questions Take the quiz below to check your understanding of Homeostasis: Open Assessments Test Yourself Check Your Understanding 1 of 2 Test Yourself What is the first step of the process that is altered for people with Diabetes Type 1?\" , \"","skipped":[{"docno":"msmarco_v2.1_doc_22_1435045666#1_3102183421","rank":1,"relevance":2},{"docno":"msmarco_v2.1_doc_22_1435045666#2_3102185121","rank":2,"relevance":2}]}}
